# BKR INFRA website — environment variables
#
# Nothing in Task 1 (scaffold, brand tokens, typography) reads process.env.
# This file is reserved for later tasks: the Sanity data source, lead-capture
# email delivery, and the /api/revalidate secret. Populate it as those tasks
# introduce real variable names — do not guess them here ahead of time.

# Task 23 (SEO, metadata, structured data): this site's own canonical origin, with no
# trailing slash. Used for metadataBase, the sitemap's absolute URLs and JSON-LD. Falls back
# to http://localhost:3000 (the same address Next.js itself already assumes once metadataBase
# is unset) when this is not set, so local dev and CI need nothing here — set it to the real
# production domain once one is registered, not before.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://www.bkrinfra.com

# Tasks 19-20 (Sanity schemas, Studio, data source). Leaving every one of these unset is a fully
# supported, tested state: activeSource() in lib/data/index.ts falls back to 'mock' and the site
# runs exactly as it does today. Set all five together, once a real Sanity project exists, to
# switch the live site over to owner-editable content.

# Safe to expose to the browser: both are needed client-side by the embedded Studio at /studio
# and by next-sanity's image URL builder, and neither grants any access on its own — a project ID
# and dataset name are not secrets, only the API token below is.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_PROJECT_ID=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_DATASET=production

# Server-only. A read token for the Sanity API (Viewer role is enough). Never prefix this with
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ — doing so would ship it to every visitor's browser and let anyone read draft/
# unpublished content directly from the Sanity API, bypassing this site's isPublished filtering
# entirely. Read only via process.env on the server (see sanity/lib/client.ts); leaving it unset
# is fine for a public dataset, but is required if the dataset is ever made private.
# SANITY_API_READ_TOKEN=

# Server-only. A shared secret this site's /api/revalidate route checks against the signature
# Sanity's outgoing webhook sends, so nothing else on the internet can trigger a revalidation.
# Never prefix this with NEXT_PUBLIC_ — that would let anyone forge a valid webhook call.
# SANITY_REVALIDATE_SECRET=
